---
/*
  KindBar — "this is a task, and here is how to make it an event instead"
  (14 · Piece 3, §6; 10-hq §4.21 as narrowed on 2026-08-04).

  ⚠ THIS IS WHAT KEEPS A ROUTER HONEST. 10-hq §4.21 forbids a model deciding
  what a captured thought IS, and the recorded reason is that a router's failure
  is SILENT — a thought filed as the wrong kind disappears into the wrong room.
  Event vs task is the one pair that argument does not cover: both render on the
  same calendar grid and both appear on Today, so a wrong guess is the wrong
  shape somewhere you are already looking.

  This bar is the rest of the answer. The guess is never silent: it is named, it
  is explained, and the other shape is one tap away — before anything is
  written. Take this bar away and the feature becomes the thing §4.21 refused.

  ⚠ THE REASON IS DERIVED, NEVER WRITTEN BY THE MODEL. Asked to explain itself,
  it fabricated: "renew the passport before the end of the month" was correctly
  called a task and justified with *"it repeats annually and asks to be warned
  in advance"* — nothing the sentence said, and contradicting the empty
  recurrence field it had just returned. Tightening the instruction did not fix
  it; removing the question did. `whyKind()` composes this line from the fields,
  so it cannot disagree with them (10-hq §10i — derived summaries beat written
  ones).

  Hidden unless a parse opened the sheet. Typing a task by hand in the Agenda
  room is not a judgement anybody made, so there is nothing to explain.
*/
interface Props {
  /** Which sheet this instance lives in — the switch offers the other one. */
  self: 'task' | 'event';
}
const { self } = Astro.props;
const other = self === 'task' ? 'event' : 'task';
---

<div class="kindbar" data-kindbar data-self={self} hidden>
  <span class="kindbar__what">{self === 'task' ? 'Task' : 'Event'}</span>
  <span class="kindbar__why" data-kind-why></span>
  <button type="button" class="kindbar__switch" data-kind-switch>
    Make it {other === 'event' ? 'an event' : 'a task'} instead
  </button>
</div>
